# ITM BRD — Requirements to Spec Bundle

You are processing a BRD for ITM. Input: **$ARGUMENTS**

The argument is a file path (`docs/hotel-workforce-brd.md`) or pasted BRD text.

## Step 0 — parse and validate the BRD

Read the BRD and look for these standard sections:
- Objectives / Goals · Scope · Functional Requirements · Non-Functional Requirements
- Constraints · Assumptions · Glossary · Stakeholders · Acceptance Criteria · Out of Scope

For each section found: extract it.
For each section missing: flag it explicitly — the human should fill these gaps.

Extract individual requirements from Functional Requirements and Acceptance Criteria. Assign tracking IDs: REQ-001, REQ-002, ...

Save parsed BRD to `specs/<feature-slug>/brd-source.md` for audit trail.

## Step 1 — run deliberation on the BRD (mandatory)

Before writing any spec:

```bash
node deliberation/cli.js \
  --proposal "Implement: <BRD title or first objective>" \
  --criteria "All REQ-xxx requirements addressable,Testable,Maintainable,Within constraints" \
  --slug "<feature-slug>"
```

The deliberation surfaces:
- Which requirements are ambiguous and need clarification
- Architectural approach for the feature set
- Risk areas the team disagrees on
- What to build first (story priority)

## Step 2 — produce the spec bundle

Read `.deliberation/<slug>/decision.md` first. Every artifact must trace to BRD requirements.

### `specs/<slug>/brief.md`
- One-page summary, link to BRD source, deliberation reference, key decisions, scope boundaries

### `specs/<slug>/prd.md`
- Requirements traceability: every functional requirement maps to a BRD REQ-xxx ID
- NFRs with measurable thresholds (latency, uptime, coverage)
- Each section ends with: `Confidence: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW`

### `specs/<slug>/architecture.md`
- Component diagram, data model sketch, integration points, ADR candidates

### `specs/<slug>/stories/*.md`
- One story per vertical slice
- Each story header: `Traces to: REQ-001, REQ-003`
- Acceptance criteria: Given/When/Then format only
- Layers affected listed explicitly

### `specs/<slug>/risk-log.md`
- Risks from deliberation DISSENT section
- Ambiguous requirements flagged during BRD parse

## Step 3 — requirements coverage report

Produce `specs/<slug>/requirements-coverage.md`:

```markdown
## Requirements coverage

| REQ ID | Requirement | Story | Status |
|--------|-------------|-------|--------|
| REQ-001 | <text> | stories/001-xxx.md | Covered |
| REQ-002 | <text> | — | NOT COVERED — requires human decision |

### Summary
- Total requirements: <n>
- Covered: <n> (<percentage>%)
- Not covered: <n> — REQUIRES HUMAN DECISION
- Deferred: <n>
```

**Every requirement must be explicitly accounted for.** Nothing gets silently dropped.

## Step 4 — open Gate 1 PR

Run verifier first. Then open PR tagged `needs-feature-approval`.

PR description must include BRD coverage summary and list any BRD sections that were missing.

## Hard stops — DevGuard blocks if:

- ❌ Skipping deliberation for "simple" BRDs
- ❌ Silently dropping requirements that don't fit the architecture
- ❌ Marking requirements as covered without a corresponding story
- ❌ Stories without REQ-xxx traceability
- ❌ Acceptance criteria without Given/When/Then format
- ❌ Missing confidence markers on PRD sections
